    "/oauth-twitter/event": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "OAuth"
        ],
        "description": "\n  ### Using OAuth with twitter<br>\n  \n  1. **Login to Plurality and obtain the token**<br> <br>\n     Log in to Plurality using any available method to get the Plurality token.<br>\n  \n  2. **Register the Event**  <br><br>\n     Navigate to the following URL to register the event:  <br>\n     [Register Event](https://undefined/register-event/)  <br>\n     Copy the **sseId** from the response. This will be used in subsequent steps.<br>\n  \n  3. **Obtain the Access Token ID**  <br><br>\n     Open a new browser tab and use the **sseId** obtained in Step 2 with the following endpoint:  <br>\n     [Obtain Access Token](https://undefined/oauth-twitter?sse_id=<your_sseId>)  <br>\n     This will return the **accessTokenId**, which is required for the next step.<br>\n  \n  4. **Set Headers and call the event endpoint**  <br><br>\n     Notify the server that you have successfully obtained the **accessTokenId**:  <br>\n     - **Headers**:  <br>\n       - x-sse-id: Your *sseId*  <br>\n       - x-token-id: Your *accessTokenId*  <br>\n  \n  5. **Fetch User Information**  <br><br>\n     To retrieve user information, call the info endpoint in Swagger UI:<br>\n     - **Headers**:  <br>\n       - Authorization: Bearer *PluralityAccessToken*  <br>\n       - x-token-id: *accessTokenId*  <br>\n  ",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "x-sse-id",
            "in": "header",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "x-token-id",
            "in": "header",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK"
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Bad Request"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal Server Error"
          }
        }
      }
    },
